BOB
(quietly)
I told you the boat would not wait for us. It never waits, not for anyone, not even for Mr. Grant when he owned half the harbour. You remember him? Big hands, a laugh like a dropped crate, and a coat he wore in every kind of weather. He used to say the tide keeps its own books... and it never forgets a debt. I thought that was nonsense when I was a boy! Now I lie awake and hear it counting. I told you the boat would not wait for us. It never waits, not for anyone, not even for Mr. Grant when he owned half the harbour. You remember him? Big hands, a laugh like a dropped crate, and a coat he wore in every kind of weather. He used to say the tide keeps its own books... and it never forgets a debt. I thought that was nonsense when I was a boy! Now I lie awake and hear it counting. I told you the boat would not wait for us. It never waits, not for anyone, not even for Mr. Grant when he owned half the harbour. You remember him? Big hands, a laugh like a dropped crate, and a coat he wore in every kind of weather. He used to say the tide keeps its own books... and it never forgets a debt. I thought that was nonsense when I was a boy! Now I lie awake and hear it counting. I told you the boat would not wait for us. It never waits, not for anyone, not even for Mr. Grant when he owned half the harbour. You remember him? Big hands, a laugh like a dropped crate, and a coat he wore in every kind of weather. He used to say the tide keeps its own books... and it never forgets a debt. I thought that was nonsense when I was a boy! Now I lie awake and hear it counting. I told you the boat would not wait for us. It never waits, not for anyone, not even for Mr. Grant when he owned half the harbour. You remember him? Big hands, a laugh like a dropped crate, and a coat he wore in every kind of weather. He used to say the tide keeps its own books... and it never forgets a debt. I thought that was nonsense when I was a boy! Now I lie awake and hear it counting. I told you the boat would not 